  "points": [
   "Pairs at 133 ms: Standard 0.331 +- 0.012 deg, Lightened 0.302 +- 0.012 (production law 0.271 / 0.244). At 167 ms: 0.264 +- 0.007 and 0.225 +- 0.005 (0.190 / 0.145). Bands beyond 233 ms are below the detector's resolution and were not used.",
   "Bursts: Standard 5/10/15 rounds 1.364 / 2.128 / 2.406 deg (production 1.169 / 1.738 / 1.973); Lightened 1.178 / 1.763 / 2.141 (1.084 / 1.532 / 1.703).",
   "All ten measurements exceed the production law. A uniform factor scale of 0.8 fits all ten (chi2 48 against 580 at 1.0; pairs prefer 0.70 to 0.75, bursts 0.80 to 0.85). A fixed dead time does not: 33 ms fits bursts only, longer pauses break bursts.",
   "Standard minus Lightened at 133 and 167 ms: 0.029 +- 0.017 and 0.039 +- 0.009 deg against 0.027 and 0.045 predicted: the x1.2 recovery operand is supported.",
   "The law's shape (per axis, clock reset on each shot, t^p) reproduces separations and group heights with one constant; the September M4A1 camera fit gave 0.77 by an independent method."
  ]
